# Copy to .env.production and set the real deployed origin.
#
# VITE_SITE_URL drives every absolute URL in the site: <link rel="canonical">,
# og:url, og:image, JSON-LD @id values and sitemap.xml. Canonical tags tell
# Google which URL is authoritative, so a wrong value here is worse than
# having none - it actively consolidates your pages onto the wrong address.
#
# Origin only. No path, no trailing slash, no trailing "/index.html".
#   good:  VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.alnanda.com.eg
#   bad:   VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.alnanda.com.eg/
#
# Until the production domain is confirmed, leave this unset. Canonicals then
# fall back to root-relative paths and `npm run verify:seo` warns instead of
# failing. `npm run verify:seo:strict` fails, which is what CI should run.
VITE_SITE_URL=
